\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Morning: CAD Weak But Off Lows After BOC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par 15:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is weaker early Monday, but off lows after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its defense against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4332 at 9:47 a.m. EST (1447 GMT), up from C$1.4340 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and from C$1.4310 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shot over C$1.4350 right around 9:00 a.m. EST (1400 GMT), prompting the BOC to step in with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and setting up a U.S. dollar move back to C$1.4329. The bank has been heavily active in the market in recent weeks, both \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and raising interest rates in an effort to contain the fallout from market turmoil in part connected to the Asian crisis. \par \par \uc2  However, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rejected calls for another rate increase Friday - the bank rate remains at 4.50% - the U.S. dollar shot through the key C$1.4285 level (70 U.S. cents), prompting heavy U.S. dollar selling from the BOC. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts think the Bank is now reluctant to raise rates again, particularly given news on Friday that inflation slowed to 0.9% in November, below its 1%-3% target range. \par \par \uc2  'The market is very thin, the bigger players are not active at the moment,' said one dealer. That may partly explain why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions this morning had a more pronounced impact. \par \par \uc2  But the trader doesn't see much improvement in the days ahead with the extent of the Asian troubles still unclear. On Monday, the Nikkei stock index in Tokyo dropped another 3.4% to its lowest level since July of 1995. \par \par \uc2  Market players fear the coming Asian economic slowdown could still cause a significant global slump, undermining Canadian exports and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:47 a.m. EST (1447 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EST (1300 GMT) and late Thursday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4332     1.4340     1.4310\par    CDN/DEM     1.2430     1.2506     1.2410\par    CDN/YEN     90.95      91.66      90.37\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1454GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcm09vhw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
