\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds Dn Slightly, Quiet Mkt Haunted By CAD Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par 15:58\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds are down slightly\par Monday morning as the market slows down for the Christmas\par holidays, with few factors at play except for some\par nervousness about the unsteady Canadian dollar.\par    "The Christmas season is really starting now," said\par David Yu, portfolio manager at Perigee Investment Counsel.\par "Most people really don't want to do much trading at this\par time," he said, adding that trades made now would have\par settlement dates falling in middle of the holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    4.75s 1999  99.19  dn 0.06  5.24% vs 5.22%\par    5.50s 2002 100.12  dn 0.09  5.47% vs 5.45%\par    7.25s 2007 111.35  dn 0.05  5.68% vs 5.67%\par    8s    2027 127.65  dn 0.05  5.99% vs 5.99%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-yr: -0.02 vs -0.05\par    CGB MAR 97 123.54  dn 0.17 volume 397\par    Yu said there is some nervousness about the Canadian\par dollar, which plunged to its lowest levels in more than 11\par years on Friday. The U.S. dollar broke through the C$1.4300\par level for the first time since early 1986 in Friday trading,\par and closed at C$1.4310 after heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par    The U.S. dollar is at C$1.4332 in mid-morning trading\par Monday, up slightly from Friday's close, but off its high of\par C$1.4351 after more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par sold U.S. dollars at C$1.4345, according to market sources.\par    Although most of the curve came down slightly in morning\par trading Monday, Yu said low volumes could exaggerate the\par impact of a single trade on the market and not too much\par significance should be attached to decline. "When the market\par is so quiet, and the volume is so thin, just one small trade\par will move it," he said.\par    The Canadian market is also taking direction from the\par mixed U.S. market Monday morning. "They're a little weaker\par in the short end, too. That may explain why our short end is\par off a bit," Yu said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  12-22-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0958EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtcm02szs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
