\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: CAD Suffers Series Of Problems \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par 15:23\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday to sell U.S. dollars at\par C$1.4345 at around 9:00 a.m. EST (1400 GMT), said traders.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under heavy downward\par pressure in the past few weeks due to a series of factors,\par prompting persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a pair of rate\par increases from the Bank of Canada in an effort to control\par the move.\par    However, the situation worsened on Friday after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rejected calls to raise interest rates once\par again, keeping its key bank rate at 4.50%. The U.S. dollar\par surged through the key C$1.4285 level (70 U.S. cents),\par putting it over 11.5-year highs and closer to an all-time\par high at C$1.4480 set in February 1986.\par    Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suffers from a combination of uncertainty\par about the economic impact from the Asian financial crisis,\par the usual thin yearend demand conditions, negative yield\par spreads to the U.S. and a current-account deficit at C$25.5\par billion in the third quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (See story on page 4227 for\par analysis of Friday's action)\par    Dealers are uncertain whether the thin conditions ahead\par of the Christmas holidays will help or hinder the Canadian\par dollar this week. Most agree more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will become\par necessary. The U.S. dollar has moved back to C$1.4238 since\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  12-22-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0923EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtcm02syu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
