\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Drops Despite BOC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1997\par 23:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar had another bad day on Thursday, dropping through a significant technical level despite the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  'It's going off the map as we talk,' said Andrew Pyle, economist with ABN Amro Hoare Govett. 'The Bank of Canada lost control of the steering wheel . . . and they're now just riding this vehicle down a very icy cliff.' \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4265 at 5:07 p.m. EST (2207 GMT), up from C$1.4214 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and from C$1.4224 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar broke through the technical level of C$1.4250 and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly after that, one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2  Pyle said three main factors were driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline Thursday: renewed concerns about the situation in Korea after the election of opposition candidate Kim Dae-Jung as president, discouraging trade numbers and speculative pressure from traders. \par \par \uc2  News that Canada's trade surplus shrank to C$581 million in October from September's revised figure of C$1.37 billion did not move the market at first. '(But) even though we didn't see an immediate response by the market to those numbers, they were very negative,' Pyle said. \par \par \uc2  Speculative buying is once again driving the Canadian dollar down as pressure mounts for another rate increase. he said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its trendsetting bank rate 1/2 point to 4.5% last Friday, but the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  took only short-term relief from the move. In the last few sessions, it has been hovering within sight of the 11-year lows - a U.S. dollar level of C$1.4290 - it hit last week. Pyle and other market watchers said the U.S. dollar could hit C$1.4300 this week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 5:07 p.m. EST (2207 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EST (1300 GMT) and late Wednesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4265     1.4214     1.4224\par    CDN/DEM     1.2442     1.2476     1.2472\par    CDN/YEN     90.17      90.11      88.64\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2212GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtci09sv3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
