\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Canada Sells -2: CAD Remains Weak Despite BOC Effort \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1997\par 21:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to sell U.S. dollars around the C$1.4250 level in an effort to stem its rise against the Canadian dollar, said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occured around 3:20 p.m. EST (2020 GMT), and is consistent with the bank's efforts in recent weeks to keep the U.S. dollar from rising above the C$1.4240-50 area. It first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this session around the C$1.4245 area starting at about 1:00 p.m. EST. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the key bank rate 1/2 point to 4.50% after repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to curtail the U.S. dollar's rise. It followed a 1/4-point rate increase on Nov. 25, a move the bank also said was to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, analysts say a variety of factors, including unsettled conditions in the Asian financial markets, still conspire to keep the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off balance and the rate increase hasn't been effective. More \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought likely as speculative sellers continue to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve in defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some observers say that a combination of weak demand typical of the yearend period, low short-term interest rates relative to those in the U.S. and a deepening current-account deficit are the other factors unsettling the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar continues to trade around C$1.4250 at 3:26 p.m. EST, from Monday's close at C$1.4202. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  12-16-97 \par \par \uc2  1532EST \par \par \uc2  4020 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtcg02syp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
