\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends stronger on Bank of Canada hike. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.4170/1.4220\tab     ASIAN CLOSE     1.4270\par RESISTANCE 1.4130   SUPPORT 1.4347\tab HI 1.4275   LO  1.4249\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN  1.4245/50    HI 1.4275     EUROPE OPEN     1.4262\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  PREV CLOSE   1.4272/77    LO 1.4130     HI 1.4264   LO  1.4244 \par \par \uc2  ----------------------MARKET COMMENT------------------------- \par \par \uc2  * Canada's dollar closed out a volatile session on Friday at C$1.4197 (US$0.7044), stronger from Thursday's close but off the session's highs. * Dealers said the trading activity tapered off after a busy morning follow the BOC rate hike. * Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was vulnerable to further weakness, depending on the behavior of Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended stronger at C$1.4197 (US$0.7044) from C$1.4272 (US$0.7007) at the close of trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The rate hike was a sharp signal by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to financial markets that it is determined to defend the Canadian dollar, which is hovering near an 11-year low. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar weakened to an 11-year low of C$1.4289 (US$0.6998) on Thursday, hurt by financial market turmoil in Asia and the reluctance of the Bank of Canada to raise interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar immediately jumped to C$1.4130 (US$70.77) after the hike, but soon began to pare gains. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased as low as C$1.4220 (US$O.7032) before the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it, buying Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars. One dealer said the market was disappointed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier to support the dollar once it began to slide. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has a slightly negative bias, but that its direction will be dictated largely by events in Asian financial markets. \par \par \uc2  "We'll wait and see how Asia reacts to the rate increase. They have their own problems to worry about. I still think you could see Canada a bit weaker," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the dollar firmed to 1.2510 marks from 1.2315 marks on Thursday, and strengthened to 91.71 yen from 90.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcc017zc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
