\par\par \b \uc2  Toronto stocks fall 1.6 percent. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lydia Zajc \par \uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1997\par 00:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Reuters) - Weak global equity markets and fears of more turbulence ahead pulled down Toronto's key stock index by 1.6 percent on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Toronto Stock Exchange's 300 Composite Index fell 109.60 points to 6644.93, faring just a little better than Wall Street's Dow Jones Industrial Average, which lost 130 points to 7849. \par \par \uc2  "I think the problem here is the spillover effect of the Asian (crises)," said Fred Ketchen, director of equity trading at ScotiaMcLeod. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell further overnight, triggering losses in equities that spilled over to other Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  In Toronto, more than 121.6 million shares changed hands, worth C$1.9 billion ($1.3 billion). \par \par \uc2  The weakness in the Canadian dollar, which dropped to 11-year lows on Thursday, also frightened investors, Ketchen said. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 70.09 U.S. cents despite heavy Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The decline prompted speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hike short-term interest rates again soon. \par \par \uc2  "We're going to hear from (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor) Gord Thiessen and the Bank of Canada in the next 48 hours," Ketchen said. \par \par \uc2  All of Toronto's 14 sub-sectors lost, led by heavy hitters conglomerates, transportation, oils and banks. \par \par \uc2  Declining issues more than doubled advancers 620 to 265, while 294 issues closed flat. \par \par \uc2  North American equities markets would remain susceptible to volatility as long as the Asian turmoil lasted, Ketchen said. \par \par \uc2  Amid hot stocks, Ranger Oil Ltd. fell 0.50 to 9.90 on 4.7 million shares and Gulfstream Resources Canada Ltd. fell 3.25 to 6.55 in light dealings. \par \par \uc2  Westmin Resources Ltd. bucked the downward trend, adding 0.05 to 5.75 in brisk trading after saying its board of directors recommended rejection of Boliden Ltd.'s C$5.40 ($3.78) a share takeover bid. Boliden fell 0.15 to 3.40. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcb015u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
