\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada continues heavy dlr buying - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in open markets on Thursday, buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at various levels after early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at C$1.4250 (US$0.7018) failed to halt its slide, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considered to be heavy. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in buying the dollar "every five points" and were in as high as C$1.4275 (US$0.7005). \par \par \uc2  The move came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to an 11-year low of C$1.4280 (US$0.7003) overnight in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the overnight move up in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on thin flows and did not reflect panic selling of the dollar. The weakness in Asia prompted to Bank of England to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight on the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began weakening off again in the North American session after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted to hold interest rates steady. Many dealers had been hoping for an interest rate hike during the bank's normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  window in order to prop up the flagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The second round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. The dollar continued to trade at C$1.4270 (US$0.7008) despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcb015tr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
