\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: C$ Weaker As Market Awaits November Jobs \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1997\par 22:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar drifted lower early Thursday and held at weaker levels throughout the session as players marked time ahead of key employment data out Friday \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4226 at 4:04 p.m. EST (2104 GMT), up from C$1.4205 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and from C$1.4192 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with one of the major Canadian banks said after pausing in its relentless rise against the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar be starting a move back up toward the C$1.4250 area. That level sparked swift \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks and 'we may see it back up there in a test to see if the bank is still around,' he said. \par \par \uc2  But much will depend on the story told in November employment numbers at 7:00 a.m. EST Friday. Traders betting that the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to for a period of strength are hoping a strong report will speed up the next rate increase. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the bank rate 1/4 point to 4.00% on Nov. 25. Some analysts think its next move will come in the new year as it moves gradually to a more neutral policy stance. \par \par \uc2  Among economists, many are betting the labor market regained its footing in November, after stumbling badly in October. (see story on page 4228). The economy remains on a strong path and it's felt that employers can't hold off long before they need to beef up staffing. Estimates range between 35,000 and 45,000 new jobs, while the unemployment is thought to have notched back to 9.0% after hitting 9.1% in October. \par \par \uc2  Also out Friday, U.S. officials release the November non-farm employment report. Dow Jones' consensus forecast has jobs up 215,000. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:04 p.m. EST (2104 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EST (1300 GMT) and late Wednesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4226     1.4205     1.4192\par    CDN/DEM     1.2446     1.2477     1.2482\par    CDN/YEN     90.89      91.05      90.66\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-12-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2108GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc409car\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
