\par\par \b \uc2  WCE nearby canola up in line with CBOT soybeans. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WINNIPEG, Dec 1 (Reuters) - WCE canola futures firmed in the nearby positions on Monday supported by a weak Canadian dollar and some commercial buying, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Nearby canola positions also garnered support from gains in Chicago Board of Trade soybean futures, an oilseeds trader said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is down a little bit and this weakness would spur more canola exports," he added. The Canadian dollar moved off its intraday lows after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying prevented a slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower levels. \par \par \uc2  January and March flax contracts fell amid some commercial profit-taking and farmer hedge selling. \par \par \uc2  At 1142 CST, January canola rose $2.00 to an offer at $399.40 a tonne, and March was up $1.90 to a bid at $403.40. January flax was off $1.70 to a bid at 344.00 and March flax lost $3.50 to a bid at $349.50. \par \par \uc2  Trading was light in western barley with commission house buying bolstering futures. The buying was capped by some local and commercial selling, a second trader said. \par \par \uc2  But he noted Friday's low at $140.00, basis December, held and on Monday, the market bounced back. There was also a rolling over of positions from December into March and May, he said. Feed wheat was mixed in light trade, he said. \par \par \uc2  At 1147 CST, December western barley offers firmed $1.10 to $145.10 and December feed wheat offers slipped $1.00 to $167.00. Feed peas and oats were lightly traded. \par \par \uc2  (All values in Canadian dollars/tonne except peas, oats.) \par \par \uc2  ((Doris Frankel, Chicago Reuters bureau 312-983-7305)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc101rao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
