\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Move Is Early, Like On Friday \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par 17:26\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in defense of the Canadian dollar again Monday, say \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, selling U.S. dollars around 10:45 a.m. EST (1545 GMT). \par \par \uc2  The move is in keeping with bank actions on Friday when it sold U.S. dollars around C$1.4245-50, well in advance of what would have normally been its usual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually only steps into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the U.S. dollar moves 70 ticks in either direction on an intraday basis. \par \par \uc2  However, both Friday and this latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have occurred at levels little changed from the previous day's close. The U.S. dollar ended Friday at C$1.4238. Traders say the action makes clear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unwilling to see the U.S. dollar weaken beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. One dealer thinks the bank is worried the U.S. dollar could test key highs at C$1.4285 (70 U.S. cents) which could spell considerable further losses for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness is a reflection of the BOC's belated response in raising rates to reduce to monetary stimulus in a robust economy, and only more rate increases will effectively cap the U.S. dollar's rise. Last Tuesday, the bank raised its bank rate 1/4 point to 4.00%. \par \par \uc2  News of a widening of the country's current-account deficit - it reached C$25.5 billion in the third quarter, over 3% of GDP and way above forecasts - also contributes to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, say analysts. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  12-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1126EST \par \par \uc2  4020 4300 4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtc102klg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
