\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Mid-Afternoon: C$ Steady After BOC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1997\par 19:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  came closer to 'drawing a line in the sand' with a surprise selling of the U.S. dollars around C$1.4245 earlier Friday, barely above the Thursday close and in a quiet and stable market. \par \par \uc2  The BOC normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when the U.S. dollar moves 70 ticks in either direction from the previous day's close. Dealers say the move (around 12:00 p.m EST) makes clear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is uncomfortable with the weak state of the Canadian dollar and is prepared to defend it: many think they'll be forced into raising rates again soon if they're really serious. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4239 at 1:39 p.m. EST (1939 GMT), from C$1.4218 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT) and from C$1.4238 late Thursday. It U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit low at C$1.4207 at 8:19 a.m. EST, but bounced back later. \par \par \uc2  'They were definitely trying to make a point and sent a strong signal,' said a dealer with a major Canadian bank. He thinks the bank has its eye on the key C$1.4285 level (70 U.S. cents) and is eager to keep the U.S. dollar below it. The rest of the session is likely to remain quiet, but any moves over C$1.4250 are thought likely to meet more BOC action. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts say the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is merely a reflection of the BOC's belated response in raising rates to reduce to monetary stimulus in a robust economy. Only more rate increases - like Tuesday's, putting the bank rate up 1/4 point to 4.0% - will effectively cap the U.S. dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  'The economy is strong enough to support higher interest rates in defense of the exchange rate,' said Andrew Spence, senior economist with Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. He said he wouldn't be surprised if the BOC raises the bank rate another 75 basis points through the January, February period. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-11-97 \par \par \uc2  1845GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbs095vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
