\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada buys Canadian dollars - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Nov 28 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday and bought Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars at the C$1.4245 (US$0.7020) level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came through brokers and was considered moderate but firm. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar weakened after the Bank of Canada disappointed many investors this morning by not delivering an interest rate hike. After the bank's normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  window passed, the dollar weakened toward the top of the overnight trading range. \par \par \uc2  It was the third straight day that the Bank of Canada bought Canadian dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after a rate hike on Tuesday failed to halt a slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to near 11-year lows. \par \par \uc2  After today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian dollar firmed to trade at C$1.4238 (US$0.7023). \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbs01x9d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal3