now debating how soon the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have tighten again. Dealers said while the near-term outlook for the Canadian dollar is bearish, the prospect of another rate hike is helping to limit losses. \par \par \uc2  "There is a certain caution in the market that we could potentially see another rate hike. People, while bullish on the (U.S.) dollar, are being careful," said Farrill. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the Canadian dollar slipped to 89.18 yen from Tuesday's close of 89.87 yen and was flat at 1.2351 marks. \par \par \uc2  ((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbq022v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
