\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Other U.S. Dlr Sellers Emerge \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par 16:09\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday selling\par U.S. dollars, said a trader. After hitting a high at\par C$1.4132 by 9:46 a.m. EST (1346 GMT), the U.S. dollar has\par since fallen back to C$1.4108 by 10:08 a.m. EST.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around C$1.4075 at\par 7:46 a.m. EST (1246 GMT) in an effort to slow the U.S.\par dollar's rise, as part of its normal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  patterns.\par The U.S. dollar closed Thursday at C$1.3994.\par    Some traders also reported selling of the U.S. dollar by\par corporate players up at the highs, helping to stall out the\par U.S. dollar rally against the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The Canadian dollar came under renewed selling pressure\par earlier Friday after news from Statistics Canada of a weak\par employment market in October. Unemployment edged back up to\par 9.1% last month, from 9.0% in September, nudged higher as\par employers shed some 11,100 jobs. Full-time employment fell\par 26,600 last month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Later reports of a strong 284,000 new jobs in the U.S.\par economy in October and a fall in the unemployment rate to\par 4.7% - the lowest level in 23 years - added to the Canadian\par dollar's troubles.\par    Market players had hoped a strong Canadian report would\par hasten the next rate increase from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par started on a "gradual" tightening path on Oct. 1 by raising\par the bank rate 1/4 point to 3.75%.\par    More volatility in the Asian equity markets overnight\par and this morning in North American stocks contributed to\par unease in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and Canadian dollar\par losses Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  11-07-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1009EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4020 4300 4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtb702e2l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
