\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: C$ Weakness After Oct. Jobs \b0\par\par\uc2 226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par 14:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday, selling the U.S. dollar\par around C$1.4075 at 7:46 a.m. EST (1246 GMT) in an effort to\par stem its rise.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tends to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Canadian\par dollar moves of 70 ticks or more from the previous day's\par close. The U.S. dollar closed Thursday at C$1.3994.\par    The Canadian dollar has come under renewed selling\par pressure after news from Statistics Canada of a weak\par employment market in October. Unemployment edged back up to\par 9.1% last month, from 9.0% in September, nudged higher as\par employers shed some 11,100 jobs. Full-time employment fell\par 26,600 last month.\par    Market players had hoped a strong report would hasten\par the next rate increase from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which started\par on a "gradual" tightening path on Oct. 1 by raising the bank\par rate 1/4 point to 3.75%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    More volatility in the Asian equity markets overnight\par also contributed to unease in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par and Canadian dollar losses Friday. Tokyo stocks plunged\par 4.2%.\par    The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4090 at 7:59 a.m. EST\par (1259 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END