\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Mid-Morning: C$ Weak, But Recovering From Worst Levels \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1997\par 17:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar remains weaker against the U.S. dollar, but is well up from the worst levels of the day Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4092 at 11:04 a.m. EST (1604 GMT), from C$1.4124 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1200 GMT) and C$1.4013 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  It hit a high Tuesday at C$1.4160, well up from a level just over C$1.3900 late last week. Throughout the run up to the high the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with U.S. dollar sales to smooth the move. \par \par \uc2  'We've seen the worst,' said Earl Johnson, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist with the Bank of Montreal in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the partial recovery results as U.S. stocks edge up from sharp early losses and take back some of the record point losses sustained in Monday's session. The Dow Jones Industrials are now up 56.97 point at 7218.12, after plunging over 550.00 points Monday. \par \par \uc2  As investors sought shelter from the stock-market rout of the past two sessions, they were also dumping Canadian dollars, U.S. dollars and Mexican pesos, in favor of other safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As the flight-to-quality reverses partially that's benefitting the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The debate now becomes, said Johnson, just to what extent the downward correction in the stock market will undermine the strength of the North American economy. If it slows growth down through a reverse 'wealth effect' it could keep the Federal Reserve on hold. 'If the Fed doesn't need to tighten anymore then that would be positive for the Canada,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers will also have an eye on the Bank of Canada. The weakening of the Canadian dollar has left monetary conditions in the economy considerably looser. Many feel the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to act soon to raise interest rates and shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It last boosted the bank rate on Oct. 1, raising it 1/4 point to 3.75%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 11:04 a.m. EST (1604 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EST (1300 GMT) and late Monday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4092     1.4124     1.4013\par    CDN/DEM     1.2264     1.2222     1.2501\par    CDN/YEN     85.02      85.15      86.85\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-10-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1616GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtas083ta\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
