\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: U.S. Dlr High At C$1.4160 \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1997\par 15:40\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday in defence\par of the Canadian dollar, this time with traders reporting bank\par selling of the U.S. dollar around the C$1.4155 level.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started early Monday as international\par investors dumped Canadian dollars and other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par favor of more stable shelter from the global stock and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sell off. The Bank of England took the baton from\par the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on its behalf overnight as\par the U.S. dollar reached a level around C$1.4155.\par    Since Friday, the U.S. dollar has climbed from levels just\par above C$1.3900 to a high of C$1.4160 overseas, reached at\par 4:06 a.m. EST (0906 GMT).\par    The U.S. dollar actually edged back to C$1.4100 as North\par American traders got to their desks. However, it quickly\par surged back toward highs after the Bank of Canada failed to\par raise interest rates at its normal operating time around 9:00\par a.m. EST.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Analysts with MMS International say a break of the spot\par high at C$1.4160 could see the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spike over\par C$1.4200, a level not seen since the Mexican peso crisis of\par 1994/95.\par    Dealers expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue its aggressive\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in its efforts to smooth out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  10-28-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0940EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4020 4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtas02amq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
