\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: C$ Plunges To Within A Hair Of Year's Lows \b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1997\par 21:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar was upended Monday as a wave of sellers pushed the U.S. dollar up to within a hair of 1997 highs at C$1.4024, prompting multiple rounds of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.4010 at 3:45 p.m. EST (2045 GMT), from C$1.3940 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1200 GMT) and C$1.3918 late Friday. It hit a high at C$1.4023 at 2:34 p.m. EST. \par \par \uc2  'The Bank of Canada has got itself into a bit of a pickle,' said a dealer with one of the major Canadian banks. Indeed, many traders said a break of C$1.4024 could set off stop-loss orders to sell the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and accelerate its decline. (see story on page 4346 for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rounds.) \par \par \uc2  Markets were rocked Monday as another sharp loss in Hong Kong stocks set the stage for a similar sell off in New York and Toronto. The Dow Jones Industrials plunged 554.26 to 7,161.15 before trading was halted, while the Toronto Stock Exchange's 300 composite index was off 434.3 points at 6,599.2. \par \par \uc2  What's more, the market faces a key test in the third-quarter employment cost (ECI) index out of the U.S. on Tuesday. If the index is strong it will fuel talk of a near-term U.S. interest rate increase, which would likely exaccerbate stock losses and the Canadian dollar's troubles. Forecasts call for a 0.8% increase. \par \par \uc2  Some observers said Canadian losses resulted as speculative investors pressed for a level at which the Bank of Canada will actually raise short-term interest rates to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It's seen vulnerable given extremely low short-term interest rates relative to the U.S. and a widening current-account deficit. (see story on page 4224) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made clear when it raised interest rates Oct. 1 that it would like to move gradually toward tighter monetary policy. However, many analysts think it is no rush to do so and particularly wants to avoid a move that is unlikely to have lingering impact on the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . 'In this sort of market it's not clear how much it would help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Mark Chandler, senior economist with Goldman Sachs Canada. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-10-97 \par \par \uc2  2046GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtar084wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
