\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dlr ends weaker despite bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.3910/1.3955\tab    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3880\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RESISTANCE 1.3805   SUPPORT 1.3955     HI 1.3885   LO  1.3875\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  CANADA OPEN  1.3885/90   HI 1.3890     EUROPE OPEN     1.3878 \par \par \uc2  PREV CLOSE   1.3882/87   LO 1.3875     HI 1.3886   LO  1.3876 \par \par \uc2  ----------------------MARKET COMMENT------------------------- \par \par \uc2  * Canada's dollar ended sharply weaker around C$1.3944 (US$0.7171) on Tuesday from Monday's close at C$1.3882 (US$0.7203), despite Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  * Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around C$1.3940 level after heavy selling by the International Monetary Market * Investors looking ahead to Canada merchandise trade data on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  Traders said tame Canadian inflation data released on Tuesday reduces the likelihood of a interest rate hike from the Bank of Canada. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders have put pressure on the Canadian dollar recently to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve. \par \par \uc2  Canada's unadjusted July consumer price index was unchanged in the month and rose 1.8 percent in the year, Statistics Canada said on Tuesday. Economists in a Reuters survey had forecast, on average, that unadjusted CPI would rise 0.1 percent on the month. "What this does is, it delays the immediate need for a rate hike from the Bank of Canada," said Goldman Sachs senior economist Mark Chandler. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't get much better in Canada. Economic activity is on the upswing while price pressures are on the downswing," Scotiabank said in a commentary on Tuesday. But it added the weak link in Canada's outlook is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate has had a hard time keeping its head above US$0.72, though lower inflation, stronger growth and substantially reduced government borrowing requirements should eventually be good news for the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Scotiabank said. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead to Wednesday, Statistics Canada is expected to report Canada's international trade and wholesale trade figures for June. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the expectation is for a wild swing so I don't think the market is going to be overly focused on it (the trade data)," said one trader at a Canadian bank. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the Canada dollar edged up to 84.74 Japanese yen from 84.66 yen on Monday and dipped to 1.3199 marks from 1.3209 marks on Monday. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8j00v4j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
