\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Soft CPI Data Weaken Cdn Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 18:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to sell the U.S. dollar around C$1.3950 around 12:08 p.m. EDT (1608 GMT) in an effort to slow its rise against the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said a trader. \par \par \uc2  As a matter of course, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has moved about 70 ticks or so in either direction on an intraday basis. The U.S. dollar closed Monday at C$1.3882, and steadily rose from there, eventually reaching the Bank of Canada's discretionary point. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said repeatedly that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is routine and not an attempt to change the direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar came under pressure earlier Tuesday soon after news that the country's core inflation rate slowed to just 1.5% in July, from 2.0% in June. Well below expectations, the figure suggests the Bank of Canada will be in no hurry to raise interest rates again - indeed, some suggest the next rate rise may be months away. With domestic short-term interest rates already still below their U.S. counterparts, that's had the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure. \par \par \uc2  Headline inflation held steady at 1.8% year over year and was flat in July from June. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-08-97 \par 