\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends weaker on broad-based selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.3750/1.3835\tab    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3778\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RESISTANCE 1.3712   SUPPORT 1.3862     HI 1.3789   LO  1.3755\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  CANADA OPEN  1.3757/62    HI 1.3833    EUROPE OPEN     1.3772 \par \par \uc2  PREV CLOSE   1.3787/92    LO 1.3752    HI 1.3772   LO  1.3752 \par \par \uc2  ---------------------MARKET COMMENT-------------------------- \par \par \uc2  * Canada's dollar ended weaker on Wednesday at C$1.3823 (US$0.7234) from Tuesday's close of C$1.3787 (US$0.7253) on broad-based, but thin selling, dealers said. * They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to levels not seen since the Bank of Canada hiked its target ceiling for the overnight financing rate to 3.50 percent on June 26. \par \par \uc2  Nasato said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had significant support around the C$1.3820 (US$0.7235) area and was not expected to weaken past C$1.3850 (US$0.7220), even if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to support the unit by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said speculation of an imminent rate hike in the U.S. may have intensified pressure on the Canadian dollar after Federal Reserve policymakers warned of the risk of higher inflation in the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Fed policymakers echoed Greenspan's comments to the Congressional panel on banking that the economy's performance was outstanding, but said the Fed must remain vigilant. \par \par \uc2  "The economy as a whole is functioning amazingly well," Fed Vice Chair Alice Rivlin told the House Banking Committee. "The overriding objective -- shared by all participants in the economy -- is to keep the good news flowing." She added that all Federal Open Market Commitee members agreed that the risk of faster inflation was "somewhat greater" than the risk of recession. \par \par \uc2  New York Fed President William McDonough said the key now was to avoid allowing the economy to avoid a boom-bust cycle. \par \par \uc2  "A U.S. rate hike would be negative for the Canadian dollar because it would lure capital flows away from Canada. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. rate hike would also put pressure on the Bank of Canada to raise interest rates here. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the Canadian dollar fell against the German mark to 1.3174 markets from 1.3222 marks at Tuesday's close. The unit rose to 83.53 yen from 83.45 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100)) \par \par \uc2  For related news, double click on one of the following: CAD/ Canadian dollar market stories CAN  Canadian news NAT  North American Treasuries news   M    Money news \par \par \uc2    D    Debt news \par \par \uc2    MF   Markets news \par \par \uc2  GVD  Government debt news MMT  Money market news INT  Interest rate news CEN  \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  news CA/BIL  Canadian weekly T-bill auction results CA/HBIL T-bill auction averages, historical rates CA/KEY  Canadian bank rate changes   CA/PA   Canadian weekly provincial T-bill auction results \par \par \uc2    CA/     Canadian bond market stories \par \par \uc2    CA/M    Canadian money market stories \par \par \uc2  CA/AUC  Canadian bond auction details   CA/MR   Canadian mortgage rates \par \par \uc2    CA/NI   New Canadian provincial and corporate debt issues \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7n0227i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
