\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Edges Higher But Seen Vulnerable \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1997\par 21:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar was higher late Friday after recovering from the day's worst levels, but it remained vulnerable to speculative attack, said traders. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar traded C$1.3742 at 3:03 p.m. EDT (1903 GMT), from C$1.3769 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and C$1.3765 late Thursday. It hit a high at C$1.3786 at 9:44 a.m. EDT. \par \par \uc2  Observers said a variety of factors contributed to the pull back from U.S. dollar highs, not least the fact that the U.S. dollar hit resistance at the day's highs. \par \par \uc2  But as the U.S. dollar took a pounding against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this session it may have help draw some buyers into Canadian dollars, said Andrew Pyle, economist with ABN Amro Hoare Govett. \par \par \uc2  He added there was also talk among some players of potential early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which many think might be growing nervous about recent Canadian dollar losses. The bank habitually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on intraday movements of 70 ticks or more in either direction. But it steps in early sometimes, as it did June 25, just a day before it last raised interest rates in defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  And its the timing of the next rate increase that will preoccupy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers as speculative type players sense the potential to force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move rates again. Pyle said if the U.S. dollar closes below C$1.3755 it might keep some speculative sellers at bay. But they'll be hovering to exploit any opportunities - it's Pyle's view that if the U.S. dollar reaches C$1.3900 or over, the Bank of Canada will again raise interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Bank watchers will have an eye on May retail sales on Monday for more clues on bank policy: some still think the economy alone might motivate the next rate increase. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 3:03 p.m. EDT (1903 GMT), from 8:00\par a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) from late Thursday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.3742     1.3769     1.3765\par    CDN/DEM     1.3048     1.3061     1.3016\par    CDN/YEN     84.20      84.09      84.05\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-07-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1905GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7i056yg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
