\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dlr ends sharply stronger after rate rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.3765/1.3840\tab     ASIAN CLOSE     1.3937\par RESISTANCE 1.3730   SUPPORT 1.3870\tab HI 1.3965   LO  1.3935\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN  1.3960/65    HI 1.3963     EUROPE OPEN     1.3959\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  PREV CLOSE   1.3935/40    LO 1.3765     HI 1.3952   LO  1.3942 \par \par \uc2  ---------------------MARKET COMMENT-------------------------- \par \par \uc2  * Canada's dollar ended more than half a U.S. cent stronger on Thursday at C$1.3815 (US$0.7238) from Wednesday's close of C$1.3935 (US$0.7176) after the Bank of Canada raised interest rates by 25 basis points, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  * The Bank of Canada raised the ceiling of its 50 basis point target range for Canada's overnight rate to 3.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement after the move that the hike was designed to "counter excessive easing in monetary conditions and to provide support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada said last month that the need for further easing in monetary conditions had largely disappeared, implying it would like to see the dollar strengthen or rates rise. \par \par \uc2  "This (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) move in the light of a 25 basis-point-hike has been incredibly dramatic. We've seen easings, we've seen tightenings, but they're usually not this violent," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the hike -- the first since February 1995 -- was likely the first of many and marked the end to a rate-cutting cycle that brought Canadians their lowest interest rates in decades. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly on Thursday to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened through key support at the C$1.3965 (US$0.7160) level. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the Canadian dollar rose to 81.81 yen from Wednesday's close of 81.68 yen and rose to 1.2480 marks from 1.2362 marks. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6q0399g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
