\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -4: Canadian Dollar Soars After Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par 23:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the Bank of Canada stepped into the market when the dollar rose C$0.0052 above Tuesday's close. Usually, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waits to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the dollar rises C$0.0070 above from the previous day's close. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and the subsequent rate hike Thursday suggest that the Bank of Canada was deeply concerned about the recent weakness of the Canadian dollar and wanted to rectify it. Amid a steady increase in payrolls, rising credit demands and a soaring stock market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deemed it could afford to tighten monetary policy to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  By all accounts, the rate increase took \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers by surprise. Expectations were that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would wait before changing monetary policy to see what course the Federal Reserve would take at the Federal Open Market Committee meeting July 2. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, 'after the dollar's rally (Wednesday), a lot people were caught short Canadian dollars,' prompting a flurry of U.S. dollar sales to cut losses, said Glenn Stevens, chief dealer at Merrill Lynch in New York. \par \par \uc2  Stevens said expects the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the Canadian dollar if the U.S. dollar falls below C$1.3770 - the intraday low posted after news of the rate hike broke. Late Thursday in New York trading, the dollar was trading at C$1.3818, down from C$1.3943 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-97 \par \par \uc2  2111GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6q04q1a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
