\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Canadian Dollar Dn Vs Dollar For 2nd Day \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1997\par 23:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  However, just as they reassessed the tankan, traders discerned mixed signals in Britain's trade report. For instance, despite the pound's rally, British exports rose 7.5% in April, suggesting British goods remain somewhat competitive. Moreover, a 9.2% increase in imports was considered further evidence that British consumer demand is booming. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar fell against the dollar for the second day in a row on indications that U.S. consumer confidence remains vibrant. U.S. existing home sales rose to their third highest level ever in May, advancing 4.4% from April. \par \par \uc2  Traders sold Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars because the data suggested that the Federal Reserve will eventually have to raise short-term U.S. rates - albeit probably not at its next meeting in early July. The Bank of Canada, by contrast, is unlikely to raise short-term Canadian rates anytime soon. Canada's three-month interest rate at 2.87% is 2.20 percentage points below the U.S. equivalent already. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the Canadian dollar's fall. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the dollar when it reached C$1.3960 - a C$0.0052 jump from its closing rate Tuesday. Usually, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waits until the dollar rises by C$0.0070 from the prior day's close. \par \par \uc2  In Asian trading, the Malaysian ringgit fell sharply against the dollar. Some traders attributed the drop to a speculative attack from overseas investors and cited heavy buying of dollars for ringgit by a U.S. hedge fund which they declined to name. \par \par \uc2  Others traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall was merely short-covering after the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a key level as well as Malaysian corporations buying dollars to square their books for first-half earnings. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-06-97 \par \par \uc2  2105GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6p04qo8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
