\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: C$ Weaker, Off Lows After BOC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1997\par 22:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar was weaker against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday, but managed a recovery from the weakest levels of the day with the Bank of Canada's (BOC) help. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading C$1.3938 at 4:38 p.m. EDT (2038 GMT), up from C$1.3926 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and C$1.3907 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Breaking with recent tradition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped in early to sell U.S. dollars as the Canadian dollar weakened, a signal said some analysts that it may be getting a bit worried about the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BOC started selling around noon when the U.S. dollar got up around C$1.3960 and continued to do so for some time, said dealers. That's just C$0.0052 above the Tuesday close, much lower than a C$0.0070 move that would have normally prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (As a loose rule the bank tends to lean against intraday moves of 70 ticks or more in either direction) \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the problem for the Canadian dollar remains the same: Canada's short-term interest rates are much lower than their U.S. counterparts, leaving investors cool, and steadily eroding interest in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 2.87%, the three-month rate is 211 basis points less than its U.S. counterpart, and few think the Bank of Canada is prepared yet to raise raise short-term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-06-97 \par \par \uc2  2026GMT \par \par \uc2  