\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of Canada Seen Growing Uneasy About  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2  By Eric Van Zant \par \uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1997\par 21:12\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Quick \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday to support the Canadian dollar may suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting nervous about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent losses - making analysts wonder whether it will soon have to raise rates in the dollar's defense. \par \par \uc2  It's feared prolonged Canadian dollar weakness may eventually overstimulate the economy by fueling the huge export sector at a time when domestic demand is already surging. Some analysts say it could take a series of rate increases to reverse the trend if the bank doesn't act soon. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be an early sign the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  is becoming uncomfortable with" the level of monetary conditions in the economy, agreed David Rosenberg, senior economist with Nesbitt Burns Inc. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling U.S. dollars around C$1.3960 just before noon EDT (1600 GMT), just C$0.0052 above Tuesday's close and well ahead of what would have been the bank's normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point this session. In routine \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only on intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements in excess of C$0.0070 in either direction. \par \par \uc2  The monetary conditions index (MCI) sits at minus 6.26, near record lows. The index measures the aggregate impact of interest rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements on monetary conditions in the economy and is an important guide to Bank of Canada policy. The lower the index, the easier monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  "I would say they are beginning to respond to the fact that the MCI is getting too easy relative to demand momentum," said Andrew Spence, senior economist with Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. \par \par \uc2  He reckons domestic demand expanded roughly 7% in the two quarters ending in March. And the demand is expected to continue to grow, not least as home owners free up funds by refinancing mortgages at low rates not seen in decades. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  06-25-97 \par \par \uc2  1512EDT \par \par \uc2  4020 4222 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt6p01cmg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
