\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Smoothing C$ Downturn \b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par 19:53\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday, selling U.S. dollars at\par about C$1.3840 around 1:20 p.m. EDT (1720 GMT), in an effort\par to smooth the fall of the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was just over 70 ticks from the Monday\par close around C$1.3768, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tends to lean\par against moves in either direction of that magnitude. It is\par not intended to influence the direction of trade, merely to\par smooth it out a bit.\par    Dealers said the downturn in the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par began early as U.S. players began selling. Some traders\par attributed the impetus for the move to a new opinion poll\par showing some slippage of voter support for the ruling Liberal\par Party as Canadian's get set for the June 2 federal election.\par    The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3826 at 1:50 p.m. EDT\par (1750 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  05-27-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1353EDT \par \par \uc2  4020 4300 4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt5r013rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
