\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Dollar Posts Sharp Gains Vs. Canadian Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par 23:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose sharply against the Canadian dollar after polls over the weekend showed the ruling Liberal Party's lead over the opposition narrowing. Canada's general election is scheduled for June 2. \par \par \uc2  Markets are concerned that the elections may produce an unclear majority in Canada's parliament. \par \par \uc2  A poll conducted by Ottawa-based Ekos Research Associates showed the Liberal Party supported by 38% of decided voters, the Progressive Conservative Party by 21%, and the Reform Party by 18%. \par \par \uc2  Another poll done by New Hartford, N.Y.-based John Zogby Group International showed the Liberals supported by 40.7% of decided voters, the Progressive Conservative Party by 22%, and the Reform Party by 18.8%. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the Canadian dollar's slide, selling U.S. dollars at about C$1.3840 around 1720 GMT. The dollar still ended higher Tuesday. At the New York close, it was trading at C$1.3843, up from C$1.3768 late in Frankfurt Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Canadian dollar's decline was made worse by the release of the U.S. consumer confidence data which raised the possibility that the gap between U.S. and Canadian rates might widen. The Canadian three-month Treasury bill currently yields 3%, about 1.98-percentage point less than its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was also hurt by the U.S. consumer confidence numbers. \par \par \uc2  'Now, if anything, it looks increasingly possible that U.S. rates will go higher while Australian rates will either stay steady or be eased again,' said Ron Leven, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan in New York. \par \par \uc2  Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its cash interest rate by 0.50 percentage point to 5.5% from 6.0% on Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-05-97 \par \par \uc2  2115GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5r03xtj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
