\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: Cdn Dollar Gets Boost From Steady Fed \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1997\par 22:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The U.S. Federal Reserve fueled another strong move in the Canadian dollar Tuesday, giving it a boost against the U.S. dollar by leaving interest rates unchanged at its policy meeting this session. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3673 at 2:48 p.m. EDT (1848 GMT), down from C$1.3737 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and C$1.3733 late Friday. It hit a low around C$1.3655 just after the Fed meeting wrapped up, and prompted smoothing Bnak of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow its rise. \par \par \uc2  'The reaction in the Canadian dollar was expected - there was no change at the Fed and the interest rates differential (between the U.S. and Canada) stayed roughly the same - it's good news for Canada,' said John Nicholson, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading with Scotia Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  At 3.03%, Canada's three-month treasury bill currently yields 206 basis points less than its U.S. counterpart - the wide spread has tended keep investors away from the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and capped its upside potential. \par \par \uc2  That said, however, the Bank of Canada provided the Canadian unit a firm underpinning last week when it signalled a readiness to raise its own official interest rates. And the lack of action at the Fed Tuesday only underscores the positive environment. \par \par \uc2  In its semi-annual monetary policy report Thursday the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said stronger economic growth is beginning to use up spare production capacity. As it does 'the bank will need to promote a less stimulative path for monetary conditions,' the central bankers wrote. Those words sparked a powerful Canadian dollar rally, taking the U.S. dollar down from over C$1.3900 at mid-week to a low around C$1.3635. \par \par \uc2  'The environment is positive for the Canadian dollar at the moment - the market likes Canada and there's good speculative interest out there to buy on any pull back,' said Nicholson. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-05-97 \par \par \uc2  2034GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5k03qei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
