\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: Cdn Dlr Continues Rally On BOC Rate Hopes \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 15:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar remains on the rallying path early Friday and in volatile trade is again approaching highs against the U.S. dollar. The move was sparked Thursday after the Bank of Canada signalled it may be prepared to raise rates in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3652 at 9:23 a.m. EDT (1323 GMT), down from C$1.3637 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and from C$1.3710 late Thursday. It hit a low at C$1.3634. \par \par \uc2  'The very clearly stated shift in focus to stronger growth, soaring money supply and the need to be 'not so stimulative' was as good a buy signal as you'll get from the Bank of Canada,' said Andrew Pyle, head of fixed-income research with ABN Amro Hoare Govett. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released its semi-annual monetary policy report early Thursday. (see story on 4225 for more analysis.\} \par \par \uc2  A dealer with one of the major Canadian banks said U.S. fund-type investors have been behind a large amount of the buying. Indeed, some dealers say the same large U.S. player that was reported buying Thursday is in again Friday . \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted its biggest intraday gain since the Quebec sovereignty referendum of Oct. 30, 1995, taking the U.S. dollar down to a low at C$1.3705, from Wednesday's close at C$1.3900. The move prompted continuous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of an effort to smooth the move. \par \par \uc2  Market players believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make its presence known once again if the U.S. dollar gets down to the C$1.3630 level. The bank tends to lean against intraday moves in either direction of about 75 ticks. \par \par \uc2  Also helping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a growing belief the U.S. Federal Reserve will not raise rates at Tuesday's policy meeting. Fear of an increase, which few believed would be matched by the Bank of Canada, was behind recent Canadian dollar weakness in the first place. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:23 a.m. EDT (1323 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT) and late Thursday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.3652      1.3637     1.3710\par    CDN/DEM     1.2466      1.2470     1.2364\par    CDN/YEN     84.54       84.67      84.43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1325GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03irr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
