\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of Canada Buying Dlrs -2: Continues Through Session \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 21:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday, buying\par U.S. dollars as the Canadian dollar surges through key\par levels and keeping to its unofficial policy to lean against\par excessive moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said a trader.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began Thursday just around 11:30 a.m EDT\par (1530 GMT) at C$1.3825-30 in the morning session, said\par dealers. The U.S. dollar closed Wednesday at C$1.3900, and\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tends to step into the market on moves more\par than 70 to 75 ticks in either direction. It is not an\par attempt to change its direction, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official have\par said in the past.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was then in repeatedly through the\par session as the U.S. dollar continued to fall, most recently\par hitting levels around C$1.3725, said the dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Analysts say the strength of the move may have been\par sparked in part after the Bank of Canada signalled in its\par semi-annual monetary policy report a greater readiness to\par raise official interest rates. (see story on 4225 for\par analysis). It's also benefits from the view that the U.S.\par Federal Reserve may not have to raise interest rates May 20.\par    Momentum built through the session as the U.S. dollar\par repeatedly broke through supports, triggering technical\par stop-loss sell orders. At 3:30 p.m. EDT (1930 GMT), the U.S.\par dollar was trading at C$1.3725. The U.S. dollar was falling\par against the Japanese yen and the German mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  05-15-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1535EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4020 4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt5f01181\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
