\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Ends Session Flat; Tone Still Weak \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1997\par 22:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended Friday's session little changed against the U.S. dollar as market players continue to test the resolve of the Bank of Canada to keep interest rates steady. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.4000 at 4:00 p.m. EDT (2000 GMT), down from C$1.4010 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), but relatively unchanged from C$1.4005 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar made its now-daily move above C$1.40, hitting a high of C$1.4025 in Europe. But a trader at a major bank in Toronto said domestic players then jumped into the market to buy Canadian dollars, helping to drag the U.S. dollar down. Traders said brisk morning activity, dominated by rumors and expectations of a rate hike, gave way to a quiet afternoon session. \par \par \uc2  'It's a standoff between the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Andrew Spence, senior economist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. \par \par \uc2  The dominant thinking in the market is that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to mitigate against quick sell offs in the Canadian dollar rather than raise interest rates, and is prepared to allow monetary conditions to loosen further. \par \par \uc2  Spence said the bank believes the positive economic and fiscal fundamentals that had many analysts calling for a strong Canadian dollar this year remain in tact, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will strengthen on its own. But he said the bank's aggressive easing in interest rates last year has dissipated some of the underlying factors, largely by driving short-term interest rates more than 200 basis points below those in the U.S. Spence believes the only way for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to recover is through a rise in interest rates by the bank. \par \par \uc2  With that unlikely, one trader said it appears that the U.S. dollar has more room to rise against the Canadian dollar in the coming session. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:00 a.m. EDT (2000 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT) and late Thursday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.4000      1.4010     1.4005\par    CDN/DEM     1.2229      1.2259     1.2313\par    CDN/YEN     89.91       89.86      89.92\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-04-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2004GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4i02sgt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
