\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds End Higher Despite Weakening Canadian Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1997\par 23:02\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Government of Canada bonds ended Monday's session higher and outperformed a fairly flat U.S. Treasury market, despite a weakening Canadian dollar that forced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third straight session in an effort to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada bonds generally managed to hold onto earlier gains in the face\par of a slide in the Canadian dollar that saw the U.S. dollar touch C$1.40\par - a level not seen in a couple of years. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets late Monday selling U.S. dollars around the C$1.3995\par level, but many dealers do not think it will prevent a break above the\par C$1.40 level.\par    4.00s 1999  97.93  up 0.07  5.16% vs 5.21%\par    7.00s 2001 102.95  up 0.07  6.22% vs 6.23%\par    7.0s  2006 100.80  up 0.05  6.88% vs 6.89%\par    9s    2025 118.64  up 0.14  7.41% vs 7.42%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-Yr: -0.09 vs -0.07\par    CGB JUN 97 112.98  up 0.16  vol.  1,181\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, Canada's bond market turned in a good day. \par \par \uc2  David Adamo, head of fixed-income research at Scotia Capital Markets, said with the 30-year bond in Canada approaching the 7.50% level, and with U.S. Treasurys relatively stable, there's some investors - mainly domestic - who believe the Canadian market represents good value. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing some cash to work in Canada," he said. \par \par \uc2  One trader at a major investment firm reiterated Adamo's comment, noting that some players in Canada see the domestic market as a buying opportunity. \par \par \uc2  But he said trading was fairly quiet for most of the session, with a buying spurt near the end coinciding with a positive move in U.S. Treasurys and the release of Canadian budget deficit figures for February. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  04-14-97 \par \par \uc2  1702EDT \par \par \uc2  1182 38700 4020 4118 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt4e00rwu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
