\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  -2: Market Anticipated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 22:29\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OTTAWA (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to try and slowdown\par the Canadian dollar's fall, as traders said the bank was\par seen selling U.S. dollars around the C$1.3940 area.\par    Many traders were expecting an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at this\par level, as the U.S. dollar strengthened from C$1.3890 late\par Wednesday to peak around C$1.3945 Thursday. Although a\par smaller move than what usually prompts \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par Canadian dollar has suffered a fairly sizeable two-day sell\par off.\par    In fact, the Canadian dollar has been udner pressure for\par several months now, ever since market players realized the\par Bank of Canada was unlikely to match any increase in U.S.\par interest rates engineered by the Federal Reserve.\par    As expected, the Fed raised rates March 25 by 25 basis\par points, and the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not follow. With\par the U.S. dollar trading around C$1.3940, the Canadian dollar\par has not been this low in about one year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The continued weakness in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen by many\par analysts as forcing the Bank of Canada to raise rates, given\par that Canadian short-term rates are about 200 basis points\par below those of the U.S. But others in the market believe the\par bank may use the sizable foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves its been\par building over the past year to try and prop up the Canadian\par dollar - which is viewed by many as undervalued at current\par levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS 04-10-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1629EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt4a00r2d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
