\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Tumbles Despite BoC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 23:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar tumbled again Thursday against the U.S. dollar, forcing the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and slow down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3945 at 5:05 p.m. EDT (2105 GMT), up from C$1.3914 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and C$1.3890 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling U.S. dollars at about C$1.3940 around 4:00 p.m. (2000 GMT) in an effort to try and resist some downward pressure on the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been under attack for several weeks, as the market assessed the Bank of Canada's decision not to match a 25 basis-point hike in the key U.S. interest rate March 25. That kept Canadian short-term rates significantly below comparable U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  'There's a downward momentum that's building for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  and relative interest rates are not helping to stem the tide at this particular stage,' said Barry Davenport, senior vice-president of treasury at Bank of Montreal. \par \par \uc2  He and other market participants said the U.S. dollar could it the C$1.40 level. 'It looks like we're going to test higher,' said one Canadian dollar trader at a U.S. bank, refering to the likelihood that the U.S. dollar was going to move up. \par \par \uc2  But Davenport cautioned the Canadian dollar might experience a bit of a rebound Friday if key U.S. data proves somewhat benign, given that investors who are short Canadian may not want to carry those positions over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-97 \par \par \uc2  2117GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4a02kfv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
