\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Bonds End Lower As Falling C$ Prompts  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1997\par 23:41\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds tumbled Thursday,\par upset as the Canadian dollar plunged through key levels,\par requiring multiple rounds of defensive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The U.S. dollar surged back over C$1.3900 this session,\par from C$1.3850 late Wednesday - eventually pulling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in at C$1.3910 to smooth the move - amid concern March\par employment figures in Canada and the U.S. Friday will further\par argue for divergent monetary policies in the two countries.\par    Last Tuesday's U.S. rate increase, unmatched by the Bank\par of Canada, brought the problem to a head and has given\par Canadian bonds a life of their own. Canada's 10-year bond has\par underperformed its U.S. counterpart all week and now yields\par just 1 basis point less.\par    4.00s 1999  98.00  dn 0.24  5.09% vs 4.98%\par    7.00s 2001 103.35  dn 0.50  6.12% vs 5.99%\par    7.0s  2006 101.10  dn 0.53  6.84% vs 6.77%\par    9s    2025 118.83  dn 0.44  7.40% vs 7.37%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  10-Yr: -0.01 vs -0.08\par    CGB JUN 97 113.35  dn 0.48  vol.  5,013\par    "There's some talk the Bank of Canada may step in to\par tighten monetary policy" given the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses, said\par David Yu, fixed-income portfolio manager with Perigee\par Investment Counsel in Toronto.\par    The closely watched monetary conditions index (MCI) -\par measure of the impact on monetary conditions of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par interest rates movements - has eased off sharply as the\par Canadian dollar fell. It now stands at minus 5.91, and many\par analysts think the bank will be inclined to raise interest\par rates if it hits minus 6, in order to rebalance conditions.\par    Such a move could actually help bonds by propping up the\par Canadian dollar. "Our international clients have been very\par concerned" with what's happening to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said a\par senior dealer with a U.S. bank in Toronto. He said overseas\par players were selling this session, across the yield curve.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 04-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1641EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1182 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt4300p6k\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (canada near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority) \cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs